Lantern Observatory: A/B/C native viewport sample source kit

Includes three unchanged native 1536x1024 scenes, exact generation prompts,
provenance metadata, exact hero placement metadata, the A/B/C comparison PNG,
review summary, original transparent hero reference, and portable rebuild code.

To keep this kit compact, the three redundant hero160_context.png files are
recreated by the included script rather than duplicated in the archive.

Rebuild: install Pillow, then run python review/build_contexts.py observatory
This writes A/hero160_context.png, B/hero160_context.png,
C/hero160_context.png and the A/B/C comparison sheet beneath the theme folder.
All inputs are relative to the script. The bundled original hero is alpha-cropped
at alpha > 30, resized to 160 pixels high with Lanczos, then composited with a
small grounding shadow at the coordinates in hero_placements.json.

SHA256_MANIFEST.json verifies archive contents. REBUILT_OUTPUT_SHA256.json
records expected rebuilt PNG hashes in the review environment. Pillow/font
version differences can affect comparison typography. The script uses DejaVu
Sans when available and falls back to a Pillow default font.

This is a presentation-only cultist viewport review. Native scenery was
not repainted, expanded or upscaled. Tall scenery is baked into the image.
No camera calibration, in-engine collision or occlusion validation is claimed.
